<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">U Nu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1907–1995</span> · Also known as Thakin Nu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">U Nu (1907–1995) was a Burmese nationalist and statesman who became the first prime minister of independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> in 1948. A leader of the Thakin movement and foreign minister in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ba-maw">Ba Maw</a>'s wartime government, he succeeded the murdered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aung-san">Aung San</a> as head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anti-fascist-peoples-freedom-league">Anti-Fascist People's Freedom League</a>. He governed, with interruptions, until General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ne-win">Ne Win</a>'s military coup of March 1962 overthrew him, and he later led an armed resistance from exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/u-nu.jpg" alt="U Nu" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Staatsgreep in Birma, premier U nu, Bestanddeelnr 913-5820.jpg:Anefo derivative work: Supakit prem · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Staatsgreep_in_Birma,_premier_U_nu,_Bestanddeelnr_913-5820_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
